#!/usr/bin/env python3
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.10"
# dependencies = []
# ///
"""yabai-organize — sort windows into workspaces.

Folio tells us what projects exist. Deterministic evidence tells us what we can
prove. Jev resolves bounded semantic ambiguity. Deterministic code decides what
to do with the answer.

    gather_state → load_folio_projects → classify_fixed_windows
    → resolve_exact_project_evidence → generate_candidates
    → resolve_ambiguous_windows (Jev, then the optional generative fallback)
    → route_general_browsers → apply_app_defaults → evict_misplaced
    → allocate_project_slots → build_plan → validate_plan → execute_plan
    → update_sketchybar → log_run

Workspaces: 1 main · 2–5 project slots · 6 notes · 7 scratch · 8 inbox · 9 media · 10 comms

Usage:
    yabai-organize [--dry-run] [--shadow] [--no-jev] [--no-legacy] [--json] [-v]
                   [--threshold X] [--dump-state FILE] [--state FILE]
    yabai-organize --report [--days N]

Environment:
    JEV_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD       accept a Jev choice at or above this (default 0.7)
    JEV_MODEL                      Jev model route (default jev-latest)
    JEV_URL                        where Jev is served: TypeSafe https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone (default)
                                   or Venice https://api.venice.ai/api/v1/decisions (also config jev_url)
    JEV_API_KEY                    or the Keychain item named by config jev_api_key_keychain
                                   (TYPESAFE_API_KEY by default; VENICE_API_KEY when served by Venice)
    YABAI_ORGANIZE_SHADOW=1        Jev answers are logged but never move a window
    YABAI_ORGANIZE_LEGACY_MODEL    the old generative model, run as a shadow on every ambiguous window
                                   after the desktop is organized; its answers only reach the log
                                   (default gpt-5.5 at openai_url; empty disables)
    YABAI_ORGANIZE_OPENAI_URL      OpenAI-compatible base URL (default http://localhost:8317/v1)
    YABAI_ORGANIZE_API_KEY         key for that endpoint (else the Keychain item named by
                                   legacy_api_key_keychain, else cliproxyapi.conf for localhost:8317)
    YABAI_ORGANIZE_CONFIG          JSON overriding DEFAULT_RULES: app routing lists, thresholds, and the
                                   legacy_model / openai_url / jev_model settings above (skhd starts us
                                   with a bare environment, so prefer this file over exported variables)
                                   (default ~/.config/yabai-organize/config.json)

Logs:  ~/.local/share/yabai-organize/runs.jsonl   one record per run: decisions, shadow answers, corrections
       ~/.local/share/yabai-organize/usage.jsonl  one token-usage line per model call
State: ~/.local/state/yabai-organize/slots.json   sticky slot → project reference
       ~/.local/state/yabai-organize/last-run.json where the last live run left every window, so the
                                                   next run can log what you moved back (corrections)

Tests: python3 -m unittest discover -s ~/etc/tests/yabai_organize
"""
from __future__ import annotations

